    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The quality of kung pao depends almost entirely on heat and timing. The prawns must hit the wok in a single layer and cook for no more than 90 seconds. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kung-pao-sauce"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "kung pao sauce"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " should be mixed and ready before anything goes into the pan. Speed is the technique here."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Optional: coat the prawns in a cornflour and egg white mixture for 10 minutes before cooking. This "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "velveting-prawns"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "velveting"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " step improves the texture noticeably. The real goal is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "wok-hei"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "wok hei "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ": get the wok as hot as it will go."
          }
        ]
      },
